; ted-readline-token-before-eof (#379): a byte >= $80 as the last byte of
; a file is stored as the first byte of a token pair, the 0 behind it as
; its second: detok reads on behind the end of the line.  Lines "x" and
; "a" + $E4 (ä, no LF), loaded under blitz2, SAVE.  Correct (the possible
; fix: the half token is dropped): line 2 is saved as "a"; the original
; saves the half token (a, $E4, 0).  (It also shows unknown tokens read
; from behind the line, "a?????..." - memory contents, not compared.)
; @file bo.bas "x\na\xe4"
; @source F bo.bas
; @expect data bo.bas "x\x00a\x00"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
